{pad:meta title='Mathematics'/}
<p class="nt-lead">Formulas written in <a href="https://asciimath.org/">AsciiMath</a> and drawn as
MathML Core - the <code>&lt;math&gt;</code> element that Chrome, Firefox and Safari draw
themselves, no script, no font to load. AsciiMath reads the way a formula is typed in an
e-mail: <code>x^2</code>, <code>a/b</code>, <code>sqrt x</code>, <code>sum_(i=1)^n</code>,
<code>alpha</code>, <code>-&gt;</code>. It is AsciiMath and not TeX because TeX's braces are PAD's
own.</p>

<p class="nt-tag">Written <code>{pad:open/}notation:math 'a/b'/{pad:close/}</code>, or with the formula between the tags,
taken as written - braces and all. <code>display='block'</code> sets it on a line of its own;
<code>alttext=</code> is what a screen reader without MathML says.</p>

{include:examples/}
